# A1/A1.2/A1_20_errands_and_places.letz
# Source: PDF slide deck "L11 a1convlotsmanmeli.pdf" (A1 Conversation course, Lesson 11)
# Vocabulary drawn from the deck's "Vocabulaire" tables and "Prepositions of place" section;
# sentences from the deck's picture-description slides, matching exercise, and train-ticket dialogue.
# (m)/(f)/(n)/(pl) gender/number markers stripped; genders confirmed via lod.lu.
# "italienesch" corrected to "italieenesch" per lod.lu suggestion.
# "Busstatioun" (not a real LOD entry) replaced with "Busarrêt" (bus stop).

@lesson A1.20 "Errands & Places"

# --- Train travel ---
@word Garen = the train stations
@word Zich = the trains
@word de Quai = the platform
@word den Depart = the departure
@word d'Arrivée = the arrival
@word den Ticket = the ticket
@word de Billjee = the travel ticket
@word Frankfurt = Frankfurt

# --- Errands & shops ---
@word Kommissioune maachen = doing errands
@word d'Papeterie = the stationer's
@word de Kiosk = the kiosk
@word d'Crèche = the nursery
@word Crèchen = the nurseries
@word d'Kleedergeschäft = the clothes shop
@word de Kleederbuttek = the clothes store
@word de Busarrêt = the bus stop
@word de Policebureau = the police station
@word d'Metrosstatioun = the underground station
@word d'Parfümerie = the perfume shop

# --- Objects ---
@word d'Pult = the desk
@word Pulter = the desks
@word Classeuren = the folders
@word den Teddybier = the teddy bear
@word d'Glace = the ice cream
@word d'Bänk = the bench

# --- People ---
@word den Här = the gentleman
@word d'Damm = the lady
@word de Bouf = the lad

# --- Prepositions of place ---
@word virun = in front of
@word ënnert = under
@word iwwert = over
@word op = on
@word an = in
@word no bei = close to
@word nobäi = nearby
@word vis-à-vis vun = opposite of

# --- Descriptive words ---
@word voll = full
@word italieenesch = Italian
@word d'Foussgängerzon = the pedestrian zone
@word de Präis = the price
@word Präisser = the prices
@word d'Differenz = the difference
@word Differenzen = the differences
@word den Ënnerscheed = the distinction

# --- Verbs ---
@word stoen = to stand
@word schwiewen = to float

